- trees: at most 8192 records [root, count, [[u,v],...]]; count positive ≤ D; each record a logical out-tree on ALL participants (|C|-1 distinct directed edges, root indegree 0, others indegree 1, all reachable); for each root v, sum of counts = r_v exactly.
- L(u,v) = sum of counts of tree records containing edge u->v.
- routes: at most 32768 records [u,v,count,recipe]; distinct participant endpoints; count in [1,D]; recipe denotes a walk from u to v; for each ordered pair, the route counts sum exactly to L(u,v).
- recipes: at most 65536 nodes; [0, link, dir] or [1, left, right]; all referenced IDs/links exist; the entire circuit acyclic and well-typed; concatenation junctions: matching end/start vertex w, w not a participant.
- load: for each directed link, sum over route records of count × (number of times the walk traverses that directed link) ≤ p*b_l.

